rch (bm25).\n```\n30 | def add_content(self, more_content):\n31 |         \"\"\"Override default behavior to add only the first line of the docstring.\n32 | \n33 |         Modified based on the part of processing docstrings in the original\n34 |         implementation of this method.\n35 | \n36 |         https://github.com/sphinx-doc/sphinx/blob/faa33a53a389f6f8bc1f6ae97d6015fa92393c4a/sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py#L609-L622\n37 |         \"\"\"\n38 |         sourcename = self.get_sourcename()\n39 |         docstrings = self.get_doc()\n40 | \n41 |         if docstrings is not None:\n42 |             if not docstrings:\n43 |                 docstrings.append([])\n44 |             # Get the first non-empty line of the processed docstring; this could lead\n45 |             # to unexpected results if the object does not have a short summary line.\n46 |             short_summary = next(\n47 |                 (s for s in self.process_doc(docstrings) if s), \"<no summary>\"\n48 |             )\n49 |             self.add_line(short_summary, sourcename, 0)\n```\n\nFound function `doc/sphinxext/autoshortsummary.py:setup`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n52 | def setup(app):\n53 |     app.add_autodocumenter(ShortSummaryDocumenter)\n```\n\nFound function `doc/api_reference.py:_get_submodule`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n21 | def _get_submodule(module_name, submodule_name):\n22 |     \"\"\"Get the submodule docstring and automatically add the hook.\n23 | \n24 |     `module_name` is e.g. `sklearn.feature_extraction`, and `submodule_name` is e.g.\n25 |     `image`, so we get the docstring and hook for `sklearn.feature_extraction.image`\n26 |     submodule. `module_name` is used to reset the current module because autosummary\n27 |     automatically changes the current module.\n28 |     \"\"\"\n29 |     lines = [\n30 |         f\".. automodule:: {module_name}.{submodule_name}\",\n31 |         f\".. currentmodule:: {module_name}\",\n32 |     ]\n33 |     return \"\\n\\n\".join(lines)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"assert_consistent_docs docstring\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  4 | import functools\n  5 | import warnings\n  6 | \n  7 | __all__ = [\"deprecated\"]\n  8 | \n  9 | \n 10 | class deprecated:\n 11 |     \"\"\"Decorator to mark a function or class as deprecated.\n 12 | \n 13 |     Issue a warning when the function is called/the class is instantiated and\n 14 |     adds a warning to the docstring.\n 15 | \n 16 |     The optional extra argument will be appended to the deprecation message\n 17 |     and the docstring. Note: to use this with the default value for extra, put\n 18 |     in an empty of parentheses:\n 19 | \n 20 |     Examples\n 21 |     --------\n 22 |     >>> from sklearn.utils import deprecated\n 23 |     >>> deprecated()\n 24 |     <sklearn.utils.deprecation.deprecated object at ...>\n 25 |     >>> @deprecated()\n 26 |     ... def some_function(): pass\n 27 | \n 28 |     Parameters\n 29 |     ----------\n 30 |     extra : str, default=''\n 31 |           To be added to the deprecation messages.\n 32 |     \"\"\"\n 33 | \n 34 |     # Adapted from https://wiki.python.org/moin/PythonDecoratorLibrary,\n 35 |     # but with many changes.\n 36 | \n 37 |     def __init__(self, extra=\"\"):\n 38 |         self.extra = extra\n```\nHint: \nThe code for class `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated` is incomplete; search `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated` for the full content if needed.\n\nFound `sklearn/utils/_pprint.py:KeyValTuple`, `sklearn/utils/_pprint.py:KeyValTuple.__repr__`, `sklearn/utils/_pprint.py:KeyValTupleParam`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"This module contains the _EstimatorPrettyPrinter class used in\n  2 | BaseEstimator.__repr__ for pretty-printing estimators\"\"\"\n  3 |