    non_deterministic : bool, default=False\n219 |         Whether the estimator is not deterministic given a fixed ``random_state``.\n220 | \n221 |     requires_fit : bool, default=True\n222 |         Whether the estimator requires to be fitted before calling one of\n223 |         `transform`, `predict`, `predict_proba`, or `decision_function`.\n224 | \n225 |     _skip_test : bool, default=False\n226 |         Whether to skip common tests entirely. Don't use this unless\n227 |         you have a *very good* reason.\n228 | \n229 |     input_tags : :class:`InputTags`\n230 |         The input data(X) tags.\n231 |     \"\"\"\n232 | \n233 |     estimator_type: str | None\n234 |     target_tags: TargetTags\n235 |     transformer_tags: TransformerTags | None = None\n236 |     classifier_tags: ClassifierTags | None = None\n237 |     regressor_tags: RegressorTags | None = None\n238 |     array_api_support: bool = False\n239 |     no_validation: bool = False\n240 |     non_deterministic: bool = False\n241 |     requires_fit: bool = True\n242 |     _skip_test: bool = False\n243 |     input_tags: InputTags = field(default_factory=InputTags)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"TargetTags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:TargetTags`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `TargetTags`.\n```\n 74 | class TargetTags:\n 75 |     \"\"\"Tags for the target data.\n 76 | \n 77 |     Parameters\n 78 |     ----------\n 79 |     required : bool\n 80 |         Whether the estimator requires y to be passed to `fit`,\n 81 |         `fit_predict` or `fit_transform` methods. The tag is ``True``\n 82 |         for estimators inheriting from `~sklearn.base.RegressorMixin`\n 83 |         and `~sklearn.base.ClassifierMixin`.\n 84 | \n 85 |     one_d_labels : bool, default=False\n 86 |         Whether the input is a 1D labels (y).\n 87 | \n 88 |     two_d_labels : bool, default=False\n 89 |         Whether the input is a 2D labels (y).\n 90 | \n 91 |     positive_only : bo